  "question": {
    "text": "Nucleophilic addition reaction will be most favoured in",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "CsayU",
      "text": "$\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\right)_{2} \\mathrm{C}=\\mathrm{O}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "oGhlM",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{CHO}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Ns2YU",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CHO}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "FiuQp",
      "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/f7G9zN15UtWp76yPv3ADyg08mr5Nei9lHPHhr7FoSz8.original.fullsize.png\">",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Aldehydes are more reactive than ketones due to $+\\mathrm{I}$ effect of $-\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$ group. There are two $-\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$ group in acetone which reduces +ve charge density on carbon atom of carbonyl group. More hindered carbonyl group becomes less reactive. So in the given case $\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CHO}$ is the right choice.",
    "image": null
  },
